  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zambia - FAPA  Technical Assistance for Zambian Small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">L&apos;objectif du projet est de soutenir la croissance et le d&#xe9;veloppement des petites et moyennes entreprises en Zambie.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the projet is to support the growth and development of the Small and Medium Enterprises in Zambia.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">L&apos;assistance technique aux petites et moyennes entreprises (PME) zambiennes vise &#xe0; renforcer la capacit&#xe9; des prestataires de services financiers et non financiers &#xe0; offrir des services appropri&#xe9;s &#xe0; un secteur des PME jusque-l&#xe0; mal desservi et principalement autochtone. Le renforcement des capacit&#xe9;s des PME ainsi que l&#x2019;am&#xe9;lioration de leur acc&#xe8;s au financement contribuent &#xe0; la richesse, &#xe0; la cr&#xe9;ation d&#x2019;emplois et &#xe0; la diversification &#xe9;conomique. Le projet comprend les composantes suivantes: a) Fourniture d&#x2019;une assistance technique &#xe0; Zanaco Bank et &#xe0; Investrust Bank pour leur permettre d&#x2019;&#xe9;valuer et d&#x2019;am&#xe9;liorer la fourniture de produits et services financiers destin&#xe9;s aux PME; (b) Formation d&apos;au moins trente (30) membres du personnel &#xe0; l&apos;&#xe9;valuation, au suivi et &#xe0; la gestion du pr&#xea;t; (c) Renforcement des capacit&#xe9;s d&apos;environ quinze (15) entreprises principales de d&#xe9;veloppement des activit&#xe9;s, de fournisseurs de services (BDSP) et de cinq (5) associations sectorielles.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The technical Assistance for Zambian Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) aims to enhance the capacities of both financial and non-financial service providers to offer appropriate services to a previously underserved and mainly indigenous SME sector. Enhancing capacities of SMEs, as well as improving their access to finance contributes to wealth, job creation and economic diversification. The Project consists of the following components: (a) Provision of technical assistance to zanaco Bank and Investrust Bank to enable them assess and improve delivery of SME financial products and services targeted af SMEs; (b) Training of at least thirty (30) staff on loan assessment, monitoring and management; (c) Capacity building of about fifteen (15) core business development, service providers (BDSPs) and five (5) sectoral associations; and (d) capacity building to about fifty-to-sixty (50 to 60) sectoral SMEs from the manufacturing, tourism, construction, and financial sectors to enable them manage their growth, increase productivity and profitability and effectively engage financial support to facilitate their growth.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">L&apos;assistance technique est destin&#xe9;e aux banques participantes et &#xe0; leur personnel. En outre, les principaux prestataires de services de d&#xe9;veloppement des entreprises et les associations professionnelles sectorielles, ainsi que les dirigeants de PME et de micro-entreprises, devraient b&#xe9;n&#xe9;ficier de ce projet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The technical assistance is for participating banks and their staff. In addition, core business development service providers and sectoral business associations, as well as SME and micro-enterprise managers, should benefit from this project.</narrative>
  </description>
